WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:11.000
Step 1: There are two kinds of Google key. An OAuth client lets each person sign in with their own Google account.

2
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:19.000
Step 2: A service account works without a sign-in, through domain-wide delegation. The centre supports both.

3
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:26.000
Step 3: In Google Cloud open Google Auth platform, then Clients.

4
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:32.000
Step 4: Click Create Client and choose Web application.

5
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Step 5: Add the centre's address followed by /api/google/callback as an authorized redirect URI.

6
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:47.000
Step 6: Click Create. Copy the client ID and the client secret into the centre's settings.

7
00:00:47.000 --> 00:00:56.000
Step 7: While the app is in testing, add every account that will sign in under Audience, Test users. Anyone else is blocked.

8
00:00:56.000 --> 00:01:04.000
Step 8: For the service account path instead: IAM and Admin, Service Accounts, Create service account, then add a JSON key.

9
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Step 9: On the card, click Sign in with Google instead.

10
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:19.000
Step 10: Choose your Workspace super admin, or your Analytics admin, and click Allow. The agent checks the access and the card turns green.
